282| \begin{remark}[Deformable systems]\label{rem:b1:systems-of-points:deformable}
283| \index{deformable system}
284| For a system that is not rigid, the kinetic energy theorem reads
285| $\Delta E_k = W_{\mathrm{ext}} + W_{\mathrm{int}}$: the internal forces do
286| work (muscles, springs, friction inside the system). The skater pulling
287| her arms in, the diver tucking, a cyclist standing on the pedals all
288| gain kinetic energy with no external work --- the center of mass
289| theorem stays true, the energy comes from inside.
290| \end{remark}
